{"content":[{"c":["GAIUS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Native of Macedonia and traveling companion of Paul during the apostle’s third missionary journey. He and Aristarchus were both seized at Ephesus during the riot caused by Demetrius the silversmith (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.19.29","r":"Acts.19.29","rawR":"Acts.19.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.19.29","value":"Acts.19.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 19:29"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Native of Derbe in Lycaonia, who traveled with Paul from Ephesus to Macedonia (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.20.4","r":"Acts.20.4","rawR":"Acts.20.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.20.4","value":"Acts.20.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 20:4"},"). Some have identified him with #1 above."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Prominent believer in Corinth and host to Paul and the whole church there (",{"href":"?bref=Rom.16.23","r":"Rom.16.23","rawR":"Rom.16.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rom.16.23","value":"Rom.16.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rom 16:23"},"). Since Romans was written in Corinth, the Gaius mentioned in ",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.1.14","r":"1Cor.1.14","rawR":"1Cor.1.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.1.14","value":"1Cor.1.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Corinthians 1:14"}," was probably the same person. If so, he was baptized by Paul."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Man to whom John addressed his third letter (",{"href":"?bref=3Jn.1.1","r":"3Jn.1.1","rawR":"3Jn.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"3Jn.1.1","value":"3Jn.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"3 Jn 1:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Gaius","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Acts 19:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.19.29","rawQueryValue":"Acts.19.29","sourceRefExact":"Acts.19.29"},{"anchorText":"Acts 20:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.20.4","rawQueryValue":"Acts.20.4","sourceRefExact":"Acts.20.4"},{"anchorText":"Rom 16:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rom.16.23","rawQueryValue":"Rom.16.23","sourceRefExact":"Rom.16.23"},{"anchorText":"1 Corinthians 1:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Cor.1.14","rawQueryValue":"1Cor.1.14","sourceRefExact":"1Cor.1.14"},{"anchorText":"3 Jn 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=3Jn.1.1","rawQueryValue":"3Jn.1.1","sourceRefExact":"3Jn.1.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"729b955132f783361711c5320b0757fd5616fb3c0ab6c29297f98a6d4f01bd5a","sourceItemName":"Gaius","sourceItemOrder":22,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Gaius","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Gaius","title":"Gaius","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}